// CommandSourceService is the wire seam behind the harness's
// `prompt.CommandSource` (engine/prompt/commandsource.go): an operator-run
// driver process serves slash-command templates alongside (NOT instead of)
// the workspace's file-backed commands — the harness composes file commands
// first, then this source, then MCP prompts. No path, directory, or root
// concept crosses this wire.
//
// Driver contract:
//   - LIVE semantics: the harness consults the source on EVERY expansion and
//     palette listing — the command set MAY change between calls (there is no
//     snapshot, deliberately matching the file expander's reads-current-files
//     discipline).
//   - GetCommandBody returns the RAW template: optional YAML frontmatter is
//     permitted and the HARNESS strips it and substitutes the placeholders
//     ($ARGUMENTS, $1, $2, ...) — expansion is NEVER driver-side, so a
//     template expands byte-identically whichever backend serves it.
//   - GetCommandBody of an unknown name MUST return NOT_FOUND; the harness
//     maps it to the normal pass-through (the raw input reaches the model
//     unchanged), never an error.
//   - A runtime fault is FAIL-SOFT harness-side (the input passes through;
//     the palette omits this source) — a transient blip must never latch a
//     command "missing" or abort a run. The build-time Probe (one
//     ListCommands round trip) is FATAL on a fault (loud-misconfig posture).
//
